title: 'Hello clientNonce: serverSig binds a nonce the CLIENT chose'
summary: Before T-016 serverSig covered only a server-chosen nonce, so a same-user process could record one genuine hello and replay it from a squatted endpoint. Now hello carries a required clientNonce (base64url 16..64 bytes, clients send 32), the result echoes it, and authServerMessage = nonce, clientNonce, endpointPath, clientApi, canonical(features). Every client (TS, CLI connectGnomon, GUI) refuses a non-echo (client-nonce-mismatch, client-local) and verifies over the nonce it SENT, never the echoed field. Domain stays gnomon:auth-server:v1 (pre-freeze; line count differs). Conformance case (c) now replays a real recorded hello verbatim and echo-rewritten; falsifier = a client that trusts the echoed nonce.
